WEBVTT

00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:07.005
From finding an animal in need to bringing the right help together. Fictional example shown.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:19.093
Start with people you trust: rescue teams, receiving clinics and nearby volunteers.

00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:41.140
Add a name, their services and permission to receive rescue calls.

00:00:41.318 --> 00:00:50.319
Save the contact. Their services remain editable whenever you need to update them.

00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:57.320
Load the example, then make the same decisions you would in your own rescue.

00:00:57.479 --> 00:01:06.480
A dog cannot put weight on its rear leg. The location and a PKR 2,000 budget are ready to review.

00:01:06.544 --> 00:01:18.545
Review the report. Describe what a successful rescue should include.

00:01:18.608 --> 00:01:27.609
Check the goal and location. Edit anything that is not right before finding help.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:35.672
Confirm the goal to check your trusted contacts for availability and prices.

00:01:35.672 --> 00:01:45.672
Greenway Rescue covers all three tasks. Its PKR 3,000 quote is above your budget.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:53.722
Keep your first offer and ask for another option. Your selected plan stays unchanged.

00:01:53.722 --> 00:02:04.723
Kindred Rescue offers the same requested tasks for PKR 1,500, within your budget.

00:02:04.776 --> 00:02:11.779
Choose the plan that works for you. You stay in control of the final approval.

00:02:11.822 --> 00:02:28.823
Open Details & history to see what each helper said about the rescue and price.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:35.871
The report keeps its replies and prices together. Return to your selected plan to approve it.

00:02:35.871 --> 00:02:45.872
Confirm the selected helper, included tasks and price limit.

00:02:45.961 --> 00:02:54.963
Approve the plan. The chosen helper is asked to confirm the agreed work and price.

00:02:54.963 --> 00:03:03.964
The helper is ready. Keep the rescue up to date as you hear from them.

00:03:04.001 --> 00:03:12.007
When the helper confirms departure, record “On the way”.

00:03:12.007 --> 00:03:20.007
Record arrival after it has been confirmed by you or the helper.

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:28.050
Mark the helper’s work as finished once their part of the rescue is complete.

00:03:28.051 --> 00:03:40.052
Add where the animal is now, and confirm that it is safe.

00:03:40.191 --> 00:03:49.192
The closing note, helper updates and conversations remain with your report.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:04:00.230
Copy a summary for the people involved. Browsers without clipboard access save a text file instead.

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:11.270
Use Switch report to return to saved cases. Opening a report preserves the existing history.

00:04:11.318 --> 00:04:21.319
Update contacts, report the next incident, and keep the right people connected.
